{
 "id": "us-tariffs-section-301",
 "chip": "301 关税",
 "kicker": "BBC中文 · 中美贸易",
 "kind": "news",
 "register": "新闻",
 "gist": "The US has proposed new tariffs on 14 trading partners, including China, the EU, Japan, South Korea and Taiwan, after a Section 301 investigation into 'structural overcapacity'. China faces the highest cap (40%), but most Chinese goods would be capped at 20%. Nothing takes effect before January, after hearings, and analysts read the move as leverage ahead of US–China talks, with the trade truce expiring on 10 January. Beijing calls it political manipulation and still holds the critical-minerals card. Experts think these tariffs will stand up in court better than the 'Liberation Day' tariffs the Supreme Court struck down. The EU rejects them, and pressure is building inside the US.",
